Sign To Speak includes a modified Kotlin adaptation of the SORT/XYXY tracking
implementation from Roboflow Trackers 2.7.0, source commit
3d1532372b46bae1e31a7f4aa3d7350482dadfb6:
https://github.com/roboflow/trackers/tree/3d1532372b46bae1e31a7f4aa3d7350482dadfb6

Modified for Sign To Speak on 2026-11-09: Kotlin/JVM implementation, four
independent scalar Kalman filters, bounded two-detection assignment, at most
64 retained hypotheses, validated hand-landmark input, timestamp/generation
lifetime, cancellation and anatomical-slot continuity diagnostics.

This is a Kotlin adaptation, not the Python package running on Android.
NumPy, SciPy, Supervision and the other Python host dependencies are not bundled
in the application. The adaptation does not perform hand detection, sign
recognition or translation and is not endorsed by Roboflow.
